  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Quiet Ledger Room",
    "overview": "Montra is a monochrome room for reading money. Paper-white canvas, white panels held by a hairline and a whisper of shadow, ink for text, for the primary action and for the one navigation pill that says where you are. Nothing in the frame is coloured for decoration. The only expressive form is the capsule: tall pale tracks with ink capsules inside them, showing how full each period was. The same capsule shape returns in the segmented control, the badges and the active navigation pill, so the chart's vocabulary is the interface's vocabulary.\n\nDensity is calm rather than sparse. Figures lead at 600 weight with tabular lining numerals; labels and context sit beneath them in a two-step grey (ink-2 for secondary text, muted for metadata). Green and red are reserved for meaning: money in and money out, favourable and unfavourable change. Every other signal is carried by weight, position and the ink-on-paper contrast.\n\nLight is the default theme. Dark is a selectable mirror that maps every role to neutral greys (no tint, no hue shift), and the `system` preference follows the OS. A `dark` preference saved before store version 1 cannot be told from the old dark default, so it is moved to light once; `light` and `system` were explicit choices and are kept. The rule lives in the UI store's migration and is repeated in the pre-paint script in `index.html` so there is no flash.\n\nCoverage today: the dashboard and the shared shell (sidebar, rail, sheet, top bar, tab bar) are composed in this system. Every other page inherits the tokens and primitives but has not been recomposed, so some still carry patterns this system does not use (the uppercase page eyebrow, the generic empty-state card). Treat those as pending migration, not as precedent.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Black, white and neutral greys; green and red only for money direction and change.",
      "The capsule (fully rounded, never shorter than it is wide) as the signature form.",
      "Three radii: 10px controls, 12px larger fields and floating layers, 16px panels; pills for everything capsule-shaped.",
      "One panel surface, never nested; depth from a hairline plus a 4% shadow.",
      "Geist throughout; money in tabular figures at 600.",
      "Light default, neutral dark mirror, every text pair at WCAG 2.2 AA in both."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Meaning-Only Colour Rule",
        "body": "Green and red mean money in, money out, favourable and unfavourable. They never decorate, never tint an icon tile, never mark a category. Colour follows meaning, not direction: rising expenses read red.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Ink Rule",
        "body": "Ink fills exactly one navigation item (the page you are on), one segment per control and the primary action. A second ink-filled control in the same group means one of them is wrong.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Faint Is Not Text Rule",
        "body": "Faint (#a3a3a0) fails text contrast; use it for placeholder glyphs only. Anything a reader must read uses muted or darker.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Money Rule",
        "body": "Every amount, percentage, date range and axis tick is set with tabular lining figures (`tnum`, `lnum`), so columns align and changing values do not jitter.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Title Speaks Rule",
        "body": "A page or panel opens with its title. No uppercase kicker or eyebrow line above it.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No-Nesting Rule",
        "body": "Panels never nest. Inside a panel, group with spacing, dividers or a sunken band.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Floating-Only Shadow Rule",
        "body": "Only content that floats over other content earns the pop shadow. Resting surfaces get the whisper or nothing.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do keep the frame monochrome: ink, white and the neutral greys carry every surface, control and chart.",
      "Do reserve positive and negative for money in, money out and favourable or unfavourable change, and let `goodWhen` decide the colour of a change, not its direction.",
      "Do draw bars as capsules: fully rounded ends, never shorter than their width, ink on a pale track.",
      "Do set every amount, percentage, date and tick in tabular lining figures.",
      "Do use 10px for controls, 12px for the large fields and floating readouts, 16px for panels, and full pills for capsule shapes.",
      "Do label any panel fed by sample data with \"Sample data · as of [date]\" and show plain dates on it.",
      "Do give every chart a keyboard path, a polite live region and a screen-reader table.",
      "Do keep text at muted (#6b6b68) or darker and input borders at control grey or darker."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't introduce an accent hue: no teal, purple, gradient, glow or tinted icon tile anywhere.",
      "Don't nest panels or add a shadow to a resting surface beyond the panel whisper.",
      "Don't fill more than one navigation item, segment or primary action per group with ink.",
      "Don't set readable text in faint.",
      "Don't put an uppercase kicker or eyebrow above a page or panel title.",
      "Don't let a narrow chart squeeze capsules below 12px; scroll instead."
